    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>Be hlafordsearwum. Ond we cwædon be hlafordsearwe, ðæt he beo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.oe.star2"/> his feores scyldig, gif he his ætsacan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.oe.star3"/> ne mihte oþþe eft on þam þrimfealdum ordale ful wære.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>[Be<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.oe.24"/> hlafordsyrwum.] And we cwædon be hlafordsearwan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.oe.25"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he wære his feores scyldig, gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.oe.1"/> he hit ætsacan ne mihte oððe on ða<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.oe.3"/></hi> ðryfealdan ordale fúl wære.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-so"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>Be hlafordsearwe. We cwædon be hlafordsearwe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he wære his feores scyldig, gif he his oðsacan ne mehte oððe eft on ðæm þreofealdu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ordale ful wære.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>De prodicione domini. Diximus de proditoribus dominorum suorum, ut sue<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.oe.23"/> ipsius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.oe.24-2"/> uitę culpabiles habeantur, si non poterit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.oe.25-2"/> abnegari, uel si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.oe.26"/> in triplici ordalio noxa compareat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="4" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="130" ed="#attenborough"/>Be hlafordsearwum<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_4.attnote.fn.4"/>. Ond we cwædon be hlafordsearwe<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_4.attnote.fn.5"/>, ðæt he beo<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_4.attnote.fn.6"/> his feores scyldig, gif he his<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_4.attnote.fn.7"/> ætsacan<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_4.attnote.fn.8"/> ne mihte oþþe eft on þam þrimfealdum<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_4.attnote.fn.9"/> ordale ful wære.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>Von Verrath (Verräthereien <hi rend="italic">H Ld</hi>) am Herrn. Und wir bestimmten über Verrath am Herrn, dass der [Missethäter] sein Leben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.de.1"/> verwirkt habe, falls er [entweder überhaupt] es nicht leugnen kann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_4.lnote.de.2"/> oder nachher im dreifachen Ordal überführt wird.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of treachery (treacheries, H Ld) against a lord. And we determined concerning treachery against a lord that the [offender] shall have forfeited his life if he either cannot deny it [at all] or is afterwards convicted in the threefold ordeal.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="131" ed="#attenborough"/>And we have declared with regard to one who is accused of plotting against his lord, that he shall forfeit his life if he cannot deny it, or [if he does deny it and] is afterwards found guilty in the threefold ordeal<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_4.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="419" ed="#whitelock"/>Concerning treachery to a lord. And we have pronounced concerning treachery to a lord, that he [who is accused] is to forfeit his life if he cannot deny it or is afterwards convicted at the three-fold ordeal.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="153"><ref target="clause:Af_4-2">Af 4.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. Af. 4, 2</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="302"><label>echo</label> <ref target="clause:Af_4-2">Af 4.2</ref> <quote>II 4 is an echo of Af 4:2</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="304"><label>rehearses; follows Alfred's sequence</label> <ref target="clause:Af_4-2">Af 4.2–5</ref> <quote>This in turn prompted rehearsal of Alfred's law on treachery to lords; the next item, on breaking into churches, may have been suggested by the fact that it was also Alfred's next topic</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">B leaves a space for the rubric; ‘Be hlafordsyrwum’ is supplied from Ld. Liebermann compares Af 4.2.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Ld; Raum für Rubrik B</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so Ld; space for a rubric B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-syr- <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-syr- Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wære <hi rend="italic">in Ld So originaler</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wære more original in Ld So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oðsacan <hi rend="italic">in So originaler</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oðsacan more original in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.oe.24-2" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.oe.25-2" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rint <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rint K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt THk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in THk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Herrenverrat 7. a; Todesstrafe 3. Den Plural ‘Verrätereien’ hat auch im Text B. Ld</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Herrenverrat 7. a; Todesstrafe 3. The plural ‘treacheries’ is also found in the text in B. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_4.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd.</hi> handhaft 5 a. 7 a; Ordal 33 c. Lesart <hi rend="italic">his oðsacan</hi> ist archaischer; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb: oð-</hi> 2; <hi rend="italic">oðberstan, -fæstan, -hleape, -stande, -swerian</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid.</hi> handhaft 5 a. 7 a; Ordal 33 c. The reading <hi rend="italic">his oðsacan</hi> is more archaic; see <hi rend="italic">Wb: oð-</hi> 2; <hi rend="italic">oðberstan, -fæstan, -hleape, -stande, -swerian</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_4.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">See note to Ine, cap. 37.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_4.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>hlafordsearwum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hlafordsearwe</hi>. So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_4.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>hlafordsearwe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hlafordsearwan</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_4.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>beo</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">wære</hi>. B, So, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_4.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>his</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hit</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_4.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>ætsacan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">oðsacan</hi>. So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_4.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>þrimfealdum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðryfealdan</hi>. B.</seg></note>
